sh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787511024506147001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\n`docs/your-first-change.md` still downloads the Gerrit hook directly, permits a small patch to bypass Gerrit, and recommends `recheck` when a failure only appears flaky. Ticket fat-leaflike-canary introduced the tutorial. Tickets sultanlike-doughty-civet and sure-starred-springtail superseded its hook and retry instructions. Current project policy requires `make hooks`, Gerrit passage for every change to main, and root-cause work for nondeterministic tests.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Replace direct hook download with the supported `make hooks` command.\n- Explain that a maintainer may sponsor a contribution while its change still passes through Gerrit before main.\n- Remove the small-patch bypass.\n- Reserve `recheck` for demonstrated environmental faults.\n- Direct nondeterministic test failures to the project debugging workflow and root-cause remediation.\n- Add a narrow documentation contract for these process requirements and run documentation link checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The tutorial installs hooks only through `make hooks`.\n- [ ] The tutorial states that every change to main passes through Gerrit.\n- [ ] Maintainer sponsorship is described without a Gerrit bypass.\n- [ ] `recheck` is reserved for demonstrated environmental faults.\n- [ ] Nondeterministic test failures direct contributors to root-cause work.\n- [ ] The focused tutorial contract and documentation link checks pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/your-first-change.md","reason":"Correct hook installation, Gerrit passage, sponsorship, and nondeterministic failure guidance."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_your_fi